.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agent-memory-local/

# Flutter / Dart
.dart_tool/
build/
*.g.dart
*.freezed.dart

# pubspec.lock IS COMMITTED, and it sat in the block above until 2026-08-09.
#
# Everything above this line is generated and genuinely disposable. A lockfile is
# also generated, which is how it got swept in, but it is the one generated file an
# APPLICATION is supposed to keep. Dart draws the line there deliberately: a library
# must work across a range of versions so it does not commit one, an application
# needs to be reproducible so it does.
#
# apps/mobile is the only app, and pubspec.yaml pins by range — `^3.3.2` means
# anything up to 4.0. Twelve or so packages are named directly; 158 end up in the
# build, 155 of them transitive. Unlocked, every build re-picks the newest match for
# all of them, so the same commit produces a different app on a different day. Two
# costs, and the second is the one that bites: a build breaks with no commit from
# anybody and the search starts in the wrong place, and — once there are Cooks — the
# app on a phone cannot be rebuilt to look at.
#
# apps/web/package-lock.json was already committed. This only ever made the Flutter
# half inconsistent with the web half.

# Web surface (apps/web) — Next.js on Cloudflare, ADR-0008 Amendment 1
node_modules/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/.open-next/
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
apps/web/.wrangler/
apps/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Supabase
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

# Python bytecode — the vendored ui-ux-pro-max skill ships Python scripts,
# so running it regenerates these next to the source.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# IDE files generated by `melos bootstrap`
.idea/
*.iml

# A REVIEW AGENT'S SCRATCH HARNESS, and the pattern is the point rather than the path.
#
# Review agents run the code they are reviewing, which means writing probes into the working tree
# while the main session is also working in it. `git add -A` then sweeps them into a commit — it
# happened twice on 2026-08-07, and the first fix was to ignore the one filename that had bitten,
# which is the same enumeration mistake the exclusion vocabulary made: it covered the case somebody
# had seen and left the class open. The second agent's probe had a different name and went straight
# through.
#
# So: anything named `zz_*` anywhere is scratch, ignored, and never a deliverable. Every agent brief
# in .claude/agents/ tells its agent to use that prefix or the session scratchpad. `zz` sorts last
# and collides with nothing.
zz_*
